<article class="env-lemma" id="03LG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03LG">Lemma <span data-tag="03LG">39.12.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $G$ be a group scheme over $S$. Let $f : Y \to X$ be a $G$-equivariant morphism between $S$-schemes endowed with $G$-actions. The rule $(\mathcal{F}, \alpha ) \mapsto (f^*\mathcal{F}, (1_ G \times f)^*\alpha )$ defines a functor from the category of $G$-equivariant quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules to the category of $G$-equivariant quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ Y$-modules. </p>
